      privLink: 'Privacy policy',
      privTitle: 'Privacy policy',
      privBody: "<p class=\"upd\">Last updated 26 September 2026.</p>\n<h3>1. Who is responsible for your data?</h3>\n<p>The site wowforever.party is run as a private hobby project by Emil Leonardsson (data controller). You can reach us through the Feedback button on the site.</p>\n<h3>2. What data do we process and why?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Name or nickname and characters</b> (name, race, class, gender, professions and roles): to show players in the list and link them to groups. This data is <b>public</b>.</li>\n<li><b>Contact detail in your registration</b> (optional): to prefill applications. It is never shown to anyone else.</li>\n<li><b>Groups</b> (name, description, play times and contact): so others can find the group and apply. A group's contact is only shown to people the group accepts.</li>\n<li><b>Applications</b> (name, chosen characters, message and contact detail): so the group owner can review and reply. Your contact is only shown to the group once they accept you.</li>\n<li><b>Feedback and reports</b> (text and optional contact): to improve the site and handle abuse.</li>\n<li><b>Technical information:</b> to stop spam and abuse, a short code is derived from your IP address. The IP address itself is not stored, and the code is deleted after a day.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Legal basis</h3>\n<p>Data you fill in and submit yourself is processed with your <b>consent</b> (GDPR Article 6(1)(a)), which you give by submitting the form. Abuse protection and security are based on our <b>legitimate interest</b> (Article 6(1)(f)) in keeping the site working and safe.</p>\n<h3>4. Who can see the data?</h3>\n<p>Public data can be seen by all visitors. Private data is only seen by the people described above. To run the site we use these service providers (processors): Supabase (database, servers in the EU), GitHub (hosting) and Cloudflare (domain and DNS). We do not sell data and do not share it with anyone else.</p>\n<p>The providers may in some cases process data outside the EU/EEA. This is then done under the EU Standard Contractual Clauses or another approved safeguard.</p>\n<h3>5. How long is the data kept?</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Registrations, characters and groups are kept until you delete them yourself. Groups with no activity are removed automatically after 180 days.</li>\n<li>Declined applications are deleted after 30 days and unanswered ones after 60 days. The contact detail in accepted applications is cleared after 60 days.</li>\n<li>Feedback and reports are deleted after one year.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>6. Your rights</h3>\n<p>You have the right to information about and access to your data, to have it corrected or deleted, to request restriction, to object to the processing and to receive your data in a readable format. You can withdraw your consent at any time. You can change or delete your registration and your group yourself on the site, and the data is then deleted immediately. For other requests, for example if you have lost your private link, contact us through Feedback.</p>\n<p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (IMY), imy.se.</p>\n<h3>7. Storage in your browser</h3>\n<p>The site uses no tracking or advertising cookies. Your browser only stores what the site needs to work: your language choice and your private links (registration, group and applications). You can clear them in your browser settings, but you then lose access to your registration on that device.</p>\n<h3>8. Age</h3>\n<p>The site is intended for people aged 13 or older.</p>\n<h3>9. Changes</h3>\n<p>We may update this text. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>",
